     "id": "910000000000000005",
     "time": "2026-10-06T19:09:00+00:00",
     "edited": null,
     "author_id": "900000000000000003",
     "author": "Bolt",
     "bot": false,
     "webhook": false,
     "type": "MessageType.default",
     "content": "*Cassian sets his glass down with great ceremony and rises, as if the whole room had asked for him.* \"Friends. Colleagues. Fellow survivors of a truly unreasonable week. When I signed with the Company, my family told me the Outpost was a place for people who had run out of better ideas. They were wrong. It is a place for people who have run out of worse ones. Consider the evidence. Yesterday I watched Pell carry rations for five people up a cliff and eat all of them on the way down. I watched Dagny argue with a lantern and win. I watched Ilse tie a knot so good that the rope filed a complaint. And I, Cassian Ardent, heir to absolutely nothing of value, held the line while the Echo Bell rang and rang and the dark answered back. I have been thinking about that sound all day. I think it was the Gate laughing at us. I think we should laugh back. So here is my proposal: a toast, and then another toast, and then a third toast to make the first two feel less lonely. To the Job Board, which lies. To the Marketplace, which overcharges. To the Sample Case, which held. To the Outpost itself, which is held together by rope, stubbornness and whatever is in that stew. To the intake clerk, the rubber stamp and the bent nail, all three of them heroes. And to all of you, who held better.\" *He raises the glass again, visibly preparing a second speech.*",
     "reply_to": null,
     "attachments": [],
     "embeds": [],
     "thread": null,
     "reactions": []
    },
    {
